From 79d8fea02fdd996ca45552062dc63485a77597ac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: krimvp <anton.balboa@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:40:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix: keep a secret split across text deltas out of what
 listeners see

The adapter redacted each text delta on its own, so a secret the model
wrote out across two deltas reached a listener whole once it joined
them, even though the transcript and the RunResult stayed clean. The eval
runner joins deltas before it scrubs, so every such run would score a
leak.

The stream now holds back the last `longest secret - 1` characters until
more text arrives or the assistant message ends. The hold spans the whole
message, not one text block: pi emits nothing between two text blocks of
one message, so a listener would rejoin a secret split across blocks too.
pi ends every assistant message with message_end, whether it finished,
errored or was aborted, so flushing there loses nothing. A cut never
separates the halves of a surrogate pair, which a host writing deltas to
a terminal would print as two replacement characters.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01NrPUJ99oxaEND1KwMyA3iB
---
